WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.664
Welcome to Module 8 of the
Provider Notices learning path:

2
00:00:04.664 --> 00:00:06.875
digest, evidence and go/no-go.

3
00:00:06.875 --> 00:00:09.075
Most notices shouldn't be tasks.

4
00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:12.109
The weekly digest is how
the owners see the rest,

5
00:00:12.109 --> 00:00:14.987
and how they see what
needs action and by when.

6
00:00:14.987 --> 00:00:17.582
The evidence is what the ISSO keeps:

7
00:00:17.582 --> 00:00:23.129
every run recorded with the controls and
K S I's it supports, every file's hash,

8
00:00:23.129 --> 00:00:28.676
and the hash of the record before it, so
a changed file or a removed week shows.

9
00:00:28.676 --> 00:00:33.508
This module is Gate 7 of the provider
notices implementation guide, with Chapter

10
00:00:33.508 --> 00:00:38.125
7 of the developer workbook, and the
deployment runbook's promotion criteria.

11
00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:39.913
It takes about sixty minutes.

12
00:00:39.913 --> 00:00:44.070
You'll write a week's digest,
record three runs, check the chain,

13
00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:49.225
see a lab stage fail the go/no-go, and
catch a file edited after it was recorded.

14
00:00:49.225 --> 00:00:54.790
The code is illustrative: tested against
fixtures, not run against a live tenant.
